// EXPECT: E0283 — a `#place` offset that is not usable (ADR-0144 §4)
//
// A field's offset is measured in bytes from the start of its aggregate, so the smallest one is
// `#place 0` and a negative value names no byte.
//
// **One** refusal here, per this directory's contract. The other shape refused by this code is an
// operand that needs evaluation, for ADR-0018 §3's ordering reason — the same limit `#align` has
// (`type-errors/075`) and the same one an array length has.
//
// Its own code beside E0282 rather than one shared "bad layout attribute", because the two
// attributes have different rules and a reader filtering by code wants to know which one they got
// wrong.
//
// **What is deliberately not refused**: two fields placed at the *same* offset, which is the point
// of the attribute (`valid/115` overlays three fields on eight bytes), and an offset that does not
// satisfy the field's alignment, which every engine handles because each computes its own
// addresses.
Negative :: struct {
    header: s64;
    value: s64 #place -8;
}

main :: () {
    n: Negative;
    n.header = 1;
}
